{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lsgy7zzo","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"structure-of-atom","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 30th January Morning Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i--t-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-w3o3q5ifkmn02ssl","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: “The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.”  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: “In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.”  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :</p>\n<p>कथन (I) : समान उर्जा वाले कक्षकों को डिजेनेरेट कक्षक कहा जाता है।</p>\n<p>कथन (II) : हाइड्रोजन परमाणु में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.389ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1056 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> एवं <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.747ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1656 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> </text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"64\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-64\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> कक्षक डिजेनेरेट कक्षक नहीं हैं।</p>\n<p>उपर्युक्त कथनों के संदर्भ में, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त उत्तर चुने :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I सही है परंतु कथन II गलत है।\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I गलत है परंतु कथन II सही है।\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II गलत हैं।\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II सही हैं।"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>अपभ्रष्ट कक्षक</strong>: जिन कक्षकों की ऊर्जा समान होती है, उन्हें अपभ्रष्ट कक्षक कहते हैं।</p>\n<p><p><strong>हाइड्रोजन-सदृश परमाणु (एकल-इलेक्ट्रॉन निकाय)</strong>: हाइड्रोजन परमाणु (या किसी एक-इलेक्ट्रॉन निकाय) में, किसी कक्षक की ऊर्जा <strong>केवल</strong> मुख्य क्वांटम संख्या <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> पर निर्भर करती है, दिगंशी क्वांटम संख्या <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> पर <em>नहीं</em>। इसलिए, समान <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> वाले सभी कक्षक (जैसे, 3s, 3p, 3d) की ऊर्जा समान होती है और वे <strong>अपभ्रष्ट</strong> होते हैं।</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>बहु-इलेक्ट्रॉन परमाणु</strong>: एक से अधिक इलेक्ट्रॉन वाले परमाणुओं में, ऊर्जा <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> पर भी निर्भर करती है (और परिरक्षण जैसे अन्य कारकों पर), इसलिए बहु-इलेक्ट्रॉन परमाणुओं में 3s, 3p, और 3d कक्षक सभी अपभ्रष्ट <strong>नहीं</strong> होते हैं।</p></p>\n\n<p>अब, आइए दिए गए कथनों का मूल्यांकन करें:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>कथन (I)</strong>: \"समान ऊर्जा वाले कक्षकों को अपभ्रष्ट कक्षक कहा जाता है।\"</p>\n<p>यह कथन परिभाषा के अनुसार <strong>सत्य</strong> है।</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>कथन (II)</strong>: \"हाइड्रोजन परमाणु में, 3p और 3d कक्षक अपभ्रष्ट कक्षक नहीं हैं।\"</p>\n<p>हाइड्रोजन परमाणु में, समान मुख्य क्वांटम संख्या <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> वाले सभी कक्षक (जैसे 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>अपभ्रष्ट होते हैं</strong>।</p>\n<p>अतः, यह कथन <strong>असत्य</strong> है।</p></p>\n\n<p>इसलिए, सही विकल्प है:</p>\n<p><strong>विकल्प A: कथन I सत्य है लेकिन कथन II असत्य है।</strong></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"quantum-numbers-and-orbitals","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: “The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.”  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: “In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.”  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>"}]}